<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ulcinj</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ulcinj is a town on the southern Adriatic coast of Montenegro near the Albanian border, with an Albanian majority. An old port, held by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> and from 1571 by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a>, it was notorious as a base of corsairs. The great powers forced its transfer to Montenegro in 1880 after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/congress-of-berlin">Congress of Berlin</a>, and its walled old town and long sandy beach now draw many visitors.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ulcinj.jpg" alt="Ulcinj" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Andrey from Russia · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ulcinj,_Montenegro_-_Sept._2010.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
